<i>Let's dance</i>

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.750
<i>And once you're captivated, kiss!</i>

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.500
<i>Good love! Good love!</i>

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.875
<i>Gravitic-love!</i>

00:01:26.875 --> 00:01:28.667
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.583
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.042
<i>Shake it love, YES!</i>

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:41.500
"Going Far Beyond"

00:01:54.375 --> 00:01:59.208
You've been working pretty hard
since about last week, huh?

00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:00.500
Yeah, I guess.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.333
What are you doing?

00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:04.708
It's still a secret.

00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:06.125
Do you need help?

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.625
No, I'm all right. Thanks.

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.792
Don't overdo it.

00:02:14.792 --> 00:02:16.208
I won't.

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:33.958
Now, regarding Six Gravity's next job...

00:02:33.958 --> 00:02:36.083
As part of the larger plan
for promoting the new song,

00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:39.333
you will be managers for a day at a certain store.

00:02:39.333 --> 00:02:40.833
Yes, sir.

00:02:40.833 --> 00:02:45.750
The store is the main branch
of Animate at Ikebukuro.

00:02:47.042 --> 00:02:49.542
Animate! On top of that...

00:02:49.542 --> 00:02:51.083
...the Ikebukuro store!

00:02:51.083 --> 00:02:55.542
Yes. You two appear to know of Animate.

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.750
Animate, huh?

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.333
I used to go sometimes on the
way home from school, remember?

00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:01.667
To buy comics.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:04.417
Oh yeah. Sounds interesting.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.125
My first part-time job in a while!

00:03:06.125 --> 00:03:07.375
Manual labor!

00:03:07.375 --> 00:03:09.333
I'm burning up!

00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:13.292
W-Wait, it's not really a part-time job,
it's work for idols...

00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:15.417
Are you listening? Can you hear me?

00:03:15.417 --> 00:03:17.833
Hey, Kakeru!

00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:19.667
Ani... mate?

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:22.042
Oh? You don't know what it is, Hajime?

00:03:22.042 --> 00:03:24.750
It's a store filled with love and dreams
and burning infatuation.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:25.333
It's known for its blue sign.

00:03:25.333 --> 00:03:27.083
"Animate"
It's known for its blue sign.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:30.000
"Burning infatuation"?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.083
Oh, I'm burning up!

00:03:32.083 --> 00:03:33.083
--This is great.
--Animate, huh? I haven't been recently.

00:03:33.083 --> 00:03:35.500
--Robot anime are the best, aren't they?
--Animate, huh? I haven't been recently.

00:03:58.708 --> 00:04:01.333
Haru, we have to wake up early tomorrow, right?

00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:03.750
Don't you think you should go to sleep soon?

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:08.250
Wow, it's unusual for <i>you </i>make tea for <i>me</i>!

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.292
Thanks.

00:04:09.292 --> 00:04:10.833
What are you doing?

00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:14.250
Checking tomorrow's schedule
and what everyone will be doing.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.500
Everyone has things they're
good and not so good at.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:18.958
That's true.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:23.292
After I started thinking about who
would be best with which jobs,

00:04:23.292 --> 00:04:25.083
I couldn't stop.

00:04:25.083 --> 00:04:29.542
Couldn't you just leave that to Mr. Tsukishiro?

00:04:29.542 --> 00:04:31.250
I could.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.167
But I like doing this kind of prep work,

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.417
so I want to do it.

00:04:35.417 --> 00:04:37.250
Oh?

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:41.417
This was what you've been
working so hard on, huh?

00:04:42.333 --> 00:04:44.750
There's more,

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.917
but I'll keep it secret for a little longer.

00:04:54.292 --> 00:04:57.333
"Limited edition box
available for preorder now!"

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.500
Good morning.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.417
Good morning!

00:05:11.417 --> 00:05:15.000
Welcome to the main branch of
Animate in Ikebukuro.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.833
I look forward to working with you, Six Gravity.

00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:20.667
I look forward to working with you!

00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:23.333
Regarding the "manager for a day" event,

00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:25.292
"Manager for a Day"
we will have Haru Yayoi as manager

00:05:25.292 --> 00:05:28.417
and the other members
of Six Gravity as employees

00:05:28.417 --> 00:05:31.917
split up between the different floors
helping with various tasks.

00:05:31.917 --> 00:05:34.917
Mr. Yayoi, the items
we discussed are ready.

00:05:34.917 --> 00:05:36.708
Oh, thank you very much.

00:05:36.708 --> 00:05:38.542
"Limited Edition Tsukiusa Bunnies"

00:05:40.083 --> 00:05:42.292
Okay everyone, listen up!

00:05:42.292 --> 00:05:43.750
Hm?

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:47.583
For this event, I didn't want
to just be manager for a day.

00:05:47.583 --> 00:05:52.333
I also thought about what other
interesting things we could do.

00:05:52.333 --> 00:05:53.333
And so,

00:05:53.333 --> 00:05:58.042
"Proposal"
the proposal I wrote that got accepted was this--

00:05:58.042 --> 00:05:59.292
"Haru"
Tsukiusa?

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:02.250
"Haru"
It's not just a regular Tsukiusa bunny...

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:06.042
Oh, it's wearing the same
clothes as an Animate employee!

00:06:06.042 --> 00:06:08.542
Hm? That's not all.

00:06:08.542 --> 00:06:09.917
This is...

00:06:09.917 --> 00:06:12.458
To commemorate the manager-for-a-day project,

00:06:12.458 --> 00:06:16.583
I thought it'd be nice to have a Tsukiusa like this.

00:06:16.583 --> 00:06:19.042
Th-There it is! Glasses bunny!

00:06:19.042 --> 00:06:20.792
It's the Haru version, huh?

00:06:20.792 --> 00:06:24.000
Wow, it's really well made.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.458
It even has a mole.

00:06:25.458 --> 00:06:28.792
I was wondering what you were
working so hard on secretly...

00:06:28.792 --> 00:06:30.167
It was this, huh?

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:34.542
Yup. I wasn't sure if the goods
would be delivered in time,

00:06:34.542 --> 00:06:37.125
so I couldn't talk about it until we were sure.

00:06:37.125 --> 00:06:38.792
Sorry, Hajime.

00:06:38.792 --> 00:06:41.708
Well, I understand the circumstances.

00:06:41.708 --> 00:06:47.625
For this event, if the Tsukiusa project
proposed by Mr. Yayoi is successful,

00:06:47.625 --> 00:06:51.458
then we will not only have the
manager-for-a-day event,

00:06:51.458 --> 00:06:54.583
but we will also hold an event
to showcase your new song.

00:06:54.583 --> 00:06:55.833
Project?

00:06:55.833 --> 00:06:57.875
What's that?

00:06:59.542 --> 00:07:01.292
This Tsukiusa bunny--

00:07:01.292 --> 00:07:03.917
That Tsukiusa bunny?

00:07:03.917 --> 00:07:08.500
If we sell one thousand here today,
we will clear the mission!

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.083
A thousand?!

00:07:10.083 --> 00:07:11.750
Wow.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.708
"Tsukiusa Bunny Manager ver."
It's a nice round number, right?

00:07:13.708 --> 00:07:18.583
If we're just looking for a round number,
I feel like ten or a hundred is fine, too...

00:07:18.583 --> 00:07:20.583
Don't worry about it.

00:07:20.583 --> 00:07:22.875
We just have to sell a thousand,

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.375
so let's all work hard together.

00:07:24.375 --> 00:07:26.250
Trying to overcome the
resistance with a smile.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:31.542
Do you have any specific ideas of how
to sell a thousand of these, Haru?

00:07:31.542 --> 00:07:35.375
I was going to have everyone
think together about that now...

00:07:35.375 --> 00:07:37.792
He's left the most important part to us...

00:07:37.792 --> 00:07:41.333
Well, the signage is already done. Ta-da!

00:07:41.333 --> 00:07:44.417
An announcement about the Tsukiusa Bunny
Manager version going on sale!

00:07:44.417 --> 00:07:45.833
And with a red frame!

00:07:45.833 --> 00:07:46.917
Red frame?

00:07:46.917 --> 00:07:49.375
It means it's an Animate exclusive.

00:07:49.375 --> 00:07:52.833
Koi, you know too much about Animate...

00:07:52.833 --> 00:07:54.792
Do you come that much?

00:07:54.792 --> 00:07:59.375
Actually, I come occasionally
whenever I have time.

00:07:59.375 --> 00:08:01.250
But a thousand...?

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.500
That's a huge number, right?

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.167
All we can do is come up with a
plan and work hard, huh?

00:08:06.167 --> 00:08:10.500
I expect a lot from your ideas.
I'm counting on you all!

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:14.083
Now, let's all work hard today!

00:08:14.083 --> 00:08:15.708
--Okay!
--Okay.

00:08:29.792 --> 00:08:31.208
Oof!

00:08:34.333 --> 00:08:36.167
Excuse us, coming through!

00:08:36.167 --> 00:08:37.917
Please clear a path!

00:08:41.292 --> 00:08:44.708
♪ Copy, copy, copy, copy, try and copy us ♪

00:08:44.708 --> 00:08:48.333
♪ Count, count, count the moons ♪

00:08:48.333 --> 00:08:51.750
♪ Copy, copy, copy, copy, copy the Managers ♪

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:55.542
--This is harder than our usual dancing!
--♪ The moon, moon, moon bunny exercises ♪

00:08:57.333 --> 00:09:00.542
First, take a deep breath!

00:09:03.458 --> 00:09:05.083
"Animate Exclusive"
"Tsukiusa Bunny Manager ver."

00:09:13.958 --> 00:09:16.500
No one will come near me...

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.583
Are you sure this is okay?

00:09:18.583 --> 00:09:20.125
It's fine.

00:09:20.125 --> 00:09:25.292
The customers seem to be having enough fun
just watching you stand here, Hajime.

00:09:25.292 --> 00:09:27.625
Oh dear.

00:09:27.625 --> 00:09:29.583
What is with this difference in our jobs...?

00:09:29.583 --> 00:09:33.417
He probably has the right people
in the right places, Koi.

00:09:35.208 --> 00:09:37.208
Do you have a moment?

00:09:37.208 --> 00:09:39.208
Yes, what is it?

00:09:39.208 --> 00:09:46.583
Well, my granddaughter from outside
the city asked me to find a CD for her...

00:09:46.583 --> 00:09:50.125
Okay, can you tell me
what the title of the CD is?

00:09:50.125 --> 00:09:55.833
Hmm... I'm sorry.
I left the note I wrote at home...

00:09:55.833 --> 00:10:05.125
I see. Let's see then... Can you tell me
anything else you remember about the CD?

00:10:05.125 --> 00:10:14.542
Let's see... The one performing in it
is a voice actor... A man... who's tall...

00:10:15.583 --> 00:10:17.917
"Voice actor" "Man" "Tall" "Very popular"
He's very popular...

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:22.417
"Voice actor" "Man" "Tall" "Very popular"
It's the CD for an anime he's in...

00:10:22.417 --> 00:10:24.500
I... see...

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.917
It's a song he sang for a

00:10:26.917 --> 00:10:29.250
"Character song for a special role"
special role or something...

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:31.417
T-This is hard...

00:10:31.417 --> 00:10:33.333
I can help if you'd like.

00:10:33.333 --> 00:10:35.625
Oh, thank you!

00:10:35.625 --> 00:10:37.917
Ma'am, this way please.

00:10:37.917 --> 00:10:39.917
Oh, thank you.

00:10:42.333 --> 00:10:47.750
With just that information, it'll definitely
take a long time to find the CD...

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:51.417
Oh yes, that one! "The <i>Kamaboko </i>Song"!

00:10:51.417 --> 00:10:52.583
Oh, good!

00:10:52.583 --> 00:10:56.375
Th-That's so fast! But "<i>kamaboko</i>"...?

00:10:56.375 --> 00:11:02.208
Shiki's in it, and part of the song
played around episode 8, I think.

00:11:02.208 --> 00:11:03.625
This one, right?

00:11:03.625 --> 00:11:05.917
It's a duet sung by Tsubasa...

00:11:05.917 --> 00:11:07.500
Then it must be this one!

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:10.167
Are there any more of the limited edition left?

00:11:10.167 --> 00:11:12.083
Let me check in the back.

00:11:13.083 --> 00:11:17.292
Excuse me, but my daughter
told me to come get this...

00:11:17.292 --> 00:11:20.250
Oh, something she preordered?

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:23.958
Let's see, it's called...

00:11:23.958 --> 00:11:26.500
We can check that at the register for you.

00:11:28.875 --> 00:11:32.958
There is a first-press bonus item for this,
so please take that, as well.

00:11:32.958 --> 00:11:34.625
Thank you very much!

00:11:37.167 --> 00:11:38.292
Oh dear.

00:11:38.292 --> 00:11:39.792
"Authorized Personnel Only"
"We can't show you the back of the stage."

00:11:40.167 --> 00:11:42.333
Yup, that turned out well.

00:11:46.917 --> 00:11:48.333
Looks good.

00:11:48.833 --> 00:11:50.833
"It's Your Guys' Fault I'm Only
Popular with My Little Sister!"

00:11:54.208 --> 00:11:55.833
Thanks for your support...

00:12:03.458 --> 00:12:04.917
Excuse me!

00:12:07.792 --> 00:12:10.417
Where's the limited edition Tsukiusa bunny?

00:12:12.625 --> 00:12:14.333
Take this one.

00:12:15.458 --> 00:12:16.875
Thanks!

00:12:20.417 --> 00:12:21.167
"Mutter... Mutter..."

00:12:21.167 --> 00:12:22.875
"Mutter... Mutter..."
Mutter... Mutter...

00:12:46.833 --> 00:12:49.083
"Thank you!"

00:13:11.042 --> 00:13:14.333
That was harder than I expected.

00:13:14.333 --> 00:13:18.250
Yeah... It wasn't just about having fun.

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:22.125
There are a lot of different products,
so the notes were really helpful!

00:13:22.125 --> 00:13:24.583
I thought the poster I made was pretty good.

00:13:24.583 --> 00:13:26.958
But then you messed it up when you laminated it.

00:13:26.958 --> 00:13:30.208
About that, Aoi... Listen to this!

00:13:30.208 --> 00:13:34.083
I practiced so much,
I'm a charismatic laminator now.

00:13:34.083 --> 00:13:36.042
What's that supposed to be?

00:13:36.042 --> 00:13:40.750
Normally, you would not be helping
this much with actually running the store...

00:13:42.125 --> 00:13:46.958
...but it was at Haru's suggestion
that it turned out like this for this event.

00:13:46.958 --> 00:13:48.292
Huh?

00:13:48.292 --> 00:13:57.000
Haru said, "We are able to sing on stage
because of all the people supporting us--

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:03.375
because of the event staff,
sound engineers, and other staff.

00:14:03.375 --> 00:14:10.333
Because of them, we are able to have
our songs heard by many people."

00:14:10.333 --> 00:14:16.292
It's easy to understand that part
because you see them first-hand,

00:14:16.292 --> 00:14:22.833
but unfortunately, it's impossible for
every single fan to see you singing on stage.

00:14:22.833 --> 00:14:27.667
For those fans who cannot come to
the concert and be there in person,

00:14:27.667 --> 00:14:31.000
you need something to bring
your songs to them in your place, right?

00:14:32.292 --> 00:14:35.500
CDs are one way to do so.

00:14:36.833 --> 00:14:40.958
CDs are displayed in stores
all around the country

00:14:40.958 --> 00:14:44.875
and in the end, they bring songs
to many more people

00:14:44.875 --> 00:14:49.917
than just those who come to the concerts.

00:14:49.917 --> 00:14:55.750
Besides the staff and others at the concerts
that you already have experience with,

00:14:55.750 --> 00:15:01.250
if you also experienced first-hand what
employees from stores like this do,

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:07.292
then maybe you can put even more
into your singing than you already are.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:20.958
That's what Haru said.

00:15:20.958 --> 00:15:23.042
All right, I understand!

00:15:23.042 --> 00:15:24.667
Leave it to me!

00:15:24.667 --> 00:15:30.917
I, Koi Kisaragi, will bring the songs and love
that go into our CDs to all our fans!

00:15:30.917 --> 00:15:33.417
Koi, you're really fired up.

00:15:33.417 --> 00:15:35.917
You should get fired up sometime, too, Arata!

00:15:35.917 --> 00:15:37.875
I'm always fired up.

00:15:37.875 --> 00:15:39.083
What part of you is?!

00:15:39.083 --> 00:15:42.375
Let's do our best for the rest
of the day, too. Right, Aoi?

00:15:43.333 --> 00:15:46.333
Yeah, let's do our best, Kakeru.

00:15:53.375 --> 00:15:54.917
Yeah!

00:16:06.125 --> 00:16:09.583
We'll put up the magazines
that went on sale today now.

00:16:09.583 --> 00:16:12.833
We'll display them in a Melon stack.

00:16:12.833 --> 00:16:14.333
"Melon stack"?

00:16:14.333 --> 00:16:16.917
It's said that they started it over at Melonbooks,

00:16:16.917 --> 00:16:19.667
so that's why it's called a Melon stack.

00:16:19.667 --> 00:16:22.750
We'll make a tower, like this.

00:16:30.958 --> 00:16:34.292
♪ Copy, copy, copy, copy, try and copy us ♪

00:16:34.292 --> 00:16:37.875
♪ Count, count, count the moons ♪

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:47.583
"Tsukiusa Bunny Manager ver.
End of Line"

00:16:52.542 --> 00:16:54.375
Only a few Tsukiusas left!

00:16:54.375 --> 00:16:56.792
Everyone, gather at the limited edition
merch area on the first floor!

00:16:56.792 --> 00:16:57.792
Roger.

00:16:58.042 --> 00:16:59.042
Roger.

00:16:59.375 --> 00:17:00.708
Roger.

00:17:01.292 --> 00:17:02.833
Roger...

00:17:14.583 --> 00:17:16.000
Here you go.

00:17:21.833 --> 00:17:23.500
Thank you very much!

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:40.042
We did it! We sold a thousand of them!

00:17:40.042 --> 00:17:44.000
Oh my, we accomplished our mission.

00:17:45.375 --> 00:17:48.083
Good work, Manager-For-A-Day.

00:17:48.083 --> 00:17:50.042
Thanks, Hajime.

00:17:50.042 --> 00:17:51.583
Thanks, everyone!

00:17:58.292 --> 00:18:00.042
Huh?

00:18:00.042 --> 00:18:01.417
This is...

00:18:03.292 --> 00:18:06.125
Thank you for coming to the store today.

00:18:06.125 --> 00:18:09.375
I am Hajime Mutsuki from Six Gravity.

00:18:09.375 --> 00:18:12.167
I am Haru Yayoi, also from Gravi.

00:18:12.167 --> 00:18:15.333
Today, I was the manager for a day.

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:19.292
Even though it was decided at the eleventh hour,

00:18:19.292 --> 00:18:24.292
thank you to those of you who
bought a limited edition Tsukiusa.

00:18:24.292 --> 00:18:26.750
Also, I also thank from
the bottom of my heart

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:31.500
our fans who supported us,
and those of you who watched us warmly

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.458
as we served customers and
did things we weren't used to.

00:18:33.458 --> 00:18:36.833
We usually receive your support from
the stage, which is a little far away,

00:18:36.833 --> 00:18:43.292
but I was really happy to be able to
spend today in the same place as you all,

00:18:43.292 --> 00:18:45.417
watching from the same point of view.

00:18:45.417 --> 00:18:51.208
I hope we have more opportunities to come
in contact with you all like this in the future.

00:18:51.208 --> 00:18:54.583
Man, there were more different
types of jobs than I expected.

00:18:54.583 --> 00:18:56.625
Wasn't it surprising, Hajime?

00:18:56.625 --> 00:19:01.250
Yeah, but it was fun. And it was worth doing.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:03.875
And we reached our goal of
selling all the Haru bunnies, too.

00:19:03.875 --> 00:19:06.833
The Haru bunny's glasses are cute, aren't they?

00:19:06.833 --> 00:19:09.625
That's true. Your essence has a certain charm.

00:19:09.625 --> 00:19:11.917
You love that "essence" bit, huh?

00:19:11.917 --> 00:19:16.125
You looked good in your
concierge clothes, too, Hajime.

00:19:16.125 --> 00:19:21.042
I've worn many different kinds
of clothes since starting this job.

00:19:21.042 --> 00:19:24.125
In some sense, I'm used to it.

00:19:24.125 --> 00:19:28.250
That's Hajime for you...
Whoops, I'd love to hear more,

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:30.542
but it looks like time's almost up.

00:19:30.542 --> 00:19:33.917
Well then, go ahead and end it, Leader.

00:19:33.917 --> 00:19:36.083
End it, huh?

00:19:36.083 --> 00:19:38.625
I'm the same as you, Haru.

00:19:38.625 --> 00:19:40.917
Because we were closer to everyone
than we have been before,

00:19:40.917 --> 00:19:44.833
I was able to feel
their passion more than ever.

00:19:44.833 --> 00:19:47.042
Their passion is pushing us forward.

00:19:47.042 --> 00:19:53.000
I think we can continue running
forward because of that passion.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.208
I truly thank you all for today.

00:19:55.208 --> 00:19:59.750
Please continue supporting Six Gravity.

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:05.958
Now then, we'll start the new song event
you've all been waiting for--

00:20:05.958 --> 00:20:09.750
Are you ready? Let's go, Six Gravity!

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:11.167
Yeah!

00:20:14.833 --> 00:20:16.458
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:20:16.458 --> 00:20:18.417
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:20:21.833 --> 00:20:23.417
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:20:23.417 --> 00:20:25.250
♪ Shakin', sugar, sugar! ♪

00:20:26.917 --> 00:20:28.917
♪ Shake it love, YES! ♪

00:20:28.917 --> 00:20:32.458
♪ I'm going crazy with longing ♪

00:20:32.458 --> 00:20:34.042
♪ Brushing back my hair ♪

00:20:34.042 --> 00:20:36.083
♪ That got wet in an instant ♪

00:20:36.083 --> 00:20:38.792
♪ Being toyed with by the warm rain ♪

00:20:38.792 --> 00:20:42.292
♪ Shall I see how far I can run? ♪

00:20:42.292 --> 00:20:44.250
♪ The prayer ♪

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:46.250
♪ That spun out ♪

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:49.167
♪ Connects to the future ♪

00:20:49.167 --> 00:20:50.083
♪ Overflowing ♪

00:20:50.083 --> 00:20:51.583
♪ The miracle of love ♪

00:20:51.583 --> 00:20:53.500
♪ The wonderful miracle ♪

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:56.292
